meta {
  name: 18 Hoeren Teil 2 has 10 questions
  type: http
  seq: 18
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/listening/exercise?modelltest=7&teil=2
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{studentAccessToken}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

script:post-response {
  // Status first. Without this an expired access token — they last fifteen
  // minutes — is reported as whatever the body assertion happens to say,
  // which sent somebody hunting for missing content that was never missing.
  if (res.getStatus() >= 400) {
    throw new Error(
      "HTTP " + res.getStatus() + ": " + JSON.stringify(res.body) +
        (res.getStatus() === 401 ? "  (re-run Student Activation / 00 Login student)" : "")
    );
  }

  if (res.body.questions.length !== 10) {
    throw new Error("Teil 2 should have 10 questions, got " + res.body.questions.length);
  }
  bru.setEnvVar("b2AudioId", res.body.audioId);
}

docs {
  telc's 5-then-10 asymmetry between Teil 1 and Teil 2: Teil 1 is five short
  monologues, Teil 2 one longer dialogue with ten statements. Getting this
  backwards would mean the import mangled the question split.

  On the cdn.lerniqo.tech question: this endpoint does not return audioUrl —
  intentionally, per ListeningExerciseDto's comment ("No durable audio URL").
  The stored audio_url (which is cdn.lerniqo.tech) only gets used server-side
  by the proxy. To actually hear it:

    1. POST {{baseUrl}}/api/listening/audio/{{b2AudioId}}/play
       (same Authorization header) — spends one play, returns
       { url: "/api/listening/audio?token=…" }.
    2. Open {{baseUrl}}<that url> in a browser tab and listen.

  That play-then-stream call isn't in this collection yet since it consumes
  a limited play count (exam_plays_allowed) — add it only when you're ready
  to actually spend a play on MT 7's Teil 2 recording.
}
